Record the Start work specification and its live check

Adds the P5b specification, docs/plans/2026-09-06-p5b-start-work-spec.md, and marks the two P5b lines in the implementation checklist done with a pointer to it. The spec states plainly, for the operator, the one exception to 'nothing is created until you accept' (one inert request issue plus one plan card are written when a plan is drafted, and why a card cannot exist without an issue), lists every decision with the file and line that now carries it, gives migration 0097's SQL and its rollback and says it is presented for approval and not applied, explains that ui and packages/shared changes are already live on the dev server while the server changes and the migration need a restart the operator approves, records a numbered runtime check with the real identifiers observed on a throwaway instance built from this working tree (201 then 200 for a repeated key, 403 for an agent key, a browser draft with one task unticked and accepted, and a second plan rejected from the Brief's deep link), gives the operator exact click steps with the real control labels, and lists what is deferred. Two things worth the operator's attention that are not this feature's code: accepting a plan that wakes several tasks for a never-run agent can hit a first-run race in ensureRuntimeState (server/src/services/heartbeat.ts:2709-2723, read-then-insert with no ON CONFLICT; four of Ada's first runs failed with duplicate key agent_runtime_state_pkey and later runs succeeded), and the full server suite has two pre-existing failing test files on this machine (chat-account-routing picks up the box's Switchboard accounts; claude-local-execute has a retry date fixture that is now in the past), neither touched by P5b.

